## A Real Shopping List

Let's build a shopping list app that adds items, shows them numbered, and tells you how many things to buy.

### Adding Items

```xiom
let list: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
list.push("milk");
list.push("eggs");
list.push("bread");
list.push("butter");
```

### Printing Numbered Items

To number items, we need a counter that changes with each loop iteration. Since a for loop doesn't give us the index, we use a while loop:

```xiom
let i: Int = 0;
while i < list.len() {
  match list.get(i) {
    Some(item) -> {
      let num = i + 1;
      io.println(string.int_to_str(num) + ". " + item);
    }
    None -> {}
  }
  i = i + 1;
}
```

### Marking Items Complete

We can "check off" an item by removing it from the list:

```xiom
match list.pop() {
  Some(item) -> io.println("Got: " + item);
  None -> io.println("List is empty!");
}
```

### Full Program

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let list: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  list.push("milk");
  list.push("eggs");
  list.push("bread");

  io.println("Shopping List:");
  let i: Int = 0;
  while i < list.len() {
    match list.get(i) {
      Some(item) -> io.println(string.int_to_str(i + 1) + ". " + item);
      None -> {}
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  io.println("Items: " + string.int_to_str(list.len()));
  return 0;
}
```

